1
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,520
I know, I know!

2
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:27,480
Once you get it, shut up and follow me!

3
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,280
Senpai, you want the window?

4
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,740
What about that bento shop you recommended?

5
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,060
We're almost there!

6
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,800
Forget that,
turn the air conditioning up more!

7
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,480
You said you wanted to ride
in an open-top car, senpai,

8
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,780
so I thought the wind hitting
us directly would feel good.

9
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,860
It wasn't this crowded the last time.

10
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:09,120
These days, with the internet and such,

11
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:11,780
information spreads in no time at all,
doesn't it.

12
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,580
We'll be waiting over 40 minutes, you know.

13
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:17,080
What are we going to do, senpai?

14
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:19,940
Do you expect us to wait
that long in this damn heat?

15
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:20,900
We're going back.

16
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:25,800
What about the lunch boxes?
We were entrusted with the money, you know.

17
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,520
Well that's...

18
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:30,080
Watermelon! Watermelon!

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,220
Delicious, fresh-from-the-farm watermelon!

20
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:38,160
Alright,
let's buy that instead and take it home.

21
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:41,020
You're serious, senpai?

22
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:43,960
Yeah, in summer,
watermelon beats rice any day.

23
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,200
Now, which one should I pick?

24
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:45,720
Nyaan.

25
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:58,180
A square watermelon! Everyone's sure to be thrilled with this.
Really? I do see square watermelons now and then, but do you have a complaint?

26
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:07,440
These corners are too right-angled, it's weird. I'm worried about the taste too.
Don't worry, it's a delicious watermelon, right?

27
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:11,580
See? I'm worried.

28
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,780
Hey, I bought this one.

29
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:15,180
Yes, thanks for your business.

30
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,280
What is this?

31
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:20,460
Weren't we going to buy everyone's lunch?

32
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,920
You can eat lunch from there anytime.

33
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,900
You may never see a square
watermelon like this again!

34
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,600
I never wanted to see one, anyway.

35
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,180
Forget that, the lunch!

36
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,600
Can't you two appreciate how
wonderful this watermelon is?

37
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,580
It's perfectly square, perfectly square!

38
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:38,260
It's just creepy.

39
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:39,840
It's kind of eerie, too.

40
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,960
It's really getting bad reviews, isn't it.

41
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,860
You mustn't judge by appearances.

42
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:48,720
You bought it because the look was funny,
didn't you?

43
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,220
Gulp.

44
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:52,160
What really matters is what's inside!

45
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,600
There's no red part at all.

46
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,840
It's completely white, isn't it?

47
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:02,480
You can't judge by color alone.
The real question is the taste.

48
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,880
It must be a delicious watermelon, for sure.

49
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:06,040
Go on, try it.

50
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,480
You want me to eat it?

51
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:08,580
Yeah.

52
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:13,720
Even if the color and shape are different,
a watermelon is still a watermelon.

53
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,600
It doesn't really look like a watermelon,
does it?

54
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,680
If anything,

55
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,820
it's more like a cucumber.

56
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:22,640
Yeah, I guess.

57
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,040
That's it,
we just need to change how we eat it.

58
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,620
Let's try spreading some miso on it.

59
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,860
This is delicious.

60
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,680
Miso goes well with this watermelon.

61
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,640
Isn't that how you eat a cucumber?

62
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:36,820
This is definitely cucumber.

63
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:40,160
We were completely fooled, senpai.

64
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:44,760
Damn it, this is the greatest humiliation since
I was tricked by the Katayama kid as a child.

65
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:47,720
Buying a watermelon with everyone's
money is what got us into this.

66
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:49,920
What's wrong with buying
watermelon in summer?

67
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:52,720
Any Japanese person eats watermelon in summer,
obviously.

68
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,860
When and who decided that?

69
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:56,680
There are people who don't eat watermelon,
you know.

70
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:59,120
I don't consider someone like that Japanese.

71
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:01,520
I eat watermelon for all three meals!

72
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:02,520
You're lying.

73
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:03,640
I'm not lying!

74
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,420
In the morning,
watermelon right when I wake up.

75
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:10,734
Watermelon at dusk, and watermelon
while watching fireworks at night,

76
00:05:10,784 --> 00:05:12,940
watermelon, watermelon,
watermelon, watermelon.

77
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:16,440
For a Japanese summer,
all you need is watermelon, nothing else.

78
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:18,700
Then prove it.

79
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:19,320
What?

80
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,040
Show us you can get by this
summer on watermelon alone.

81
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,720
Not that you could.

82
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,600
Fine, I'll do it.

83
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:29,600
But if I do, you pay me one million yen.

84
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,760
Deal.

85
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:32,940
Reiko-san.

86
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:35,620
This is bad. If Chief Ohara finds out...

87
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:39,540
You'll be back in one week.

88
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:42,420
So the period is one week, got it.

89
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,860
What, only one week?

90
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:49,480
But in that week,
you'll have to eat 300 watermelons.

91
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,520
What? 300?

92
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:57,200
300 in a week works out to about 43 a day.

93
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,480
If you take away 8 hours of sleep,

94
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,760
that's just under 3 an hour.

95
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:06,820
If you can do that,
I'll pay you 1 million yen.

96
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:07,660
Well? What do you say?

97
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,760
Alright, I accept your challenge!

98
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,920
A man who'll eat 300
watermelons in one week!

99
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:24,840
Then I'll have surveillance
cameras installed so you can't cheat.

100
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,000
If you tamper with the cameras,
you're disqualified.

101
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,580
Is it okay to sprinkle
salt on the watermelon?

102
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:31,300
Seasonings are fine.

103
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,280
Drinks are okay too.

104
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,920
But if you put any food other than watermelon in your mouth,
you're out.

105
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,040
Got it.

106
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:40,780
The start time is exactly 1 p.m.

107
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:43,100
5

108
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,040
4

109
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:45,060
3

110
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:46,020
2

111
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:46,940
1

112
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,220
Go!

113
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,140
First, the classic way to eat it.

114
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,940
Eat it all at once.

115
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:02,540
Spit out all the seeds at once.

116
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,420
Ugh, how disgusting.

117
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:06,640
Spitting seeds goes with watermelon,
you know.

118
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:13,740
I'm back from patrol.

119
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:15,940
Which one is this now?

120
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,180
It's my tenth.

121
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,760
That's a pace of five an hour.

122
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:24,860
At this rate, I could do 500 or even 600!

123
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,020
Looks like you'll be paying
out the 1 million yen, Reiko.

124
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:28,840
Reiko-san...

125
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:31,140
You think you can tell that yet?

126
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:36,120
You've already eaten 80?

127
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:39,120
This way, I'll get my 1 million yen.

128
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:42,300
And I won't spend anything on food meanwhile.
Two birds with one stone!

129
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,520
That's quite a way of eating.

130
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:47,600
This way, I can eat faster.

131
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,920
Looks like you didn't manage
to spit out the seeds, though.

132
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,560
Just leave it,
and they'll come out on their own.

133
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,860
That may be true, but...

134
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,560
You've already eaten 80 of them?

135
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:58,900
220 left.

136
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,920
This is going by in no time.

137
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:04,200
Physical condition... 219 left.

138
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:08,120
Ryo-chan,
you've still left some red parts behind.

139
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:08,740
Hey.

140
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:14,600
At this rate, I can't possibly
accept that you've finished one.

141
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:18,200
Fine, fine. You're such a
stickler for the small details.

142
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,100
Here you go, Kei-chan, barley tea.

143
00:08:25,260 --> 00:08:26,680
Thanks, Reiko.

144
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:30,160
Look, in the past hour
you've only eaten two.

145
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,760
He's definitely lost his momentum.

146
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:39,940
Hey, the next one's number 100

147
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:44,160
Even this green-and-black striped
pattern is getting boring to look at.

148
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,240
That's right!

149
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,820
What are you doing, senpai?

150
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:52,920
Just a little change of pace.

151
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:55,740
Look, a red polka-dot watermelon on white.

152
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,240
That's creepy.

153
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:01,400
A soccer ball watermelon
commemorating the Best 16.

154
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:08,260
A "discovery point" watermelon with the characters
"Jin-gi-re-chi-chu-shin-ko-teri" on it.

155
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:10,020
There's more.

156
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,540
A pattern watermelon and
a psychedelic watermelon.

157
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:16,120
A space watermelon and
a melon-style watermelon.

158
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:20,360
And to top it all off,
a tricolor dango watermelon!

159
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:24,540
Alright, my appetite's come roaring back!

160
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,860
But the inside's just a
normal watermelon, right?

161
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,520
Well, of course.

162
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:44,180
Thirty yesterday alone, apparently.

163
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:46,420
Your pace has really slowed down.

164
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:49,040
It's going to slow down
even more from here on.

165
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:51,980
Ryo-sama.

166
00:09:52,840 --> 00:09:53,980
I've heard about it.

167
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:57,120
Apparently they've adjusted it so
you eat 300 watermelons in one week.

168
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:58,540
Well, yeah.

169
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:01,840
Isn't there anything I can help you with?

170
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:05,440
Even so,
we can't have someone else eat them for you.

171
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:07,660
All I can do is peel them.

172
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,920
You're good at cooking, aren't you.

173
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:18,440
I've prepared the watermelon to
look like bath-scrubbing daikon.

174
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:20,820
Somehow that makes me want to eat.

175
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,120
Let's see, let's see.

176
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,840
Mmmmmm

177
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,780
It's just watermelon with dressing on it

178
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,680
Mmmmmm

179
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:46,160
How about some watermelon juice?

180
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:48,500
This one's surprisingly good.

181
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:49,420
Thank goodness.

182
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:53,100
But it's just watermelon juice,
so you'll get tired of it fast.

183
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,680
Sorry.

184
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,380
Mmmm.

185
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,820
After all this, it's only three?

186
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:04,260
Sorry, I'm not much help.

187
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,340
Why don't you make jam?

188
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:08,600
Watermelon jam?

189
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:13,180
You have to evaporate the water out of it,
so you'd need a ton of watermelon for that.

190
00:11:13,180 --> 00:11:15,140
I'll give it a try, though.

191
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:17,380
Good, make a lot of it.

192
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:22,220
Guess I'll taste-test one.

193
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,480
How is it, Ryo-sama?

194
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:30,440
The sweetness of the
watermelon is concentrated.

195
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,640
It's hard to eat it like this.

196
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:36,000
Come to think of it, I should have
some bread I bought four days ago.

197
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:36,900
Dip it in that.

198
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:40,540
If you eat anything other than watermelon,
you're disqualified, right?

199
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:43,860
Then we have no choice but to use only jam.

200
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:44,620
Damn it!

201
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,700
Where's Senpai?

202
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:56,060
He went out on patrol. Looks like he's
sick of even looking at watermelon.

203
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:07,020
I've got a mountain of good watermelons!

204
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:16,780
But I want to eat something other than watermelon.
Something other than watermelon.

205
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:19,980
Itadakimasu!

206
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:22,020
What is this?

207
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:23,260
What do you mean?

208
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:24,680
It's ramen, obviously.

209
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,140
Ryo-san ordered it.

210
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:26,760
What?

211
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,600
Me?

212
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,100
Don't you remember?

213
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:29,580
No way.

214
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:33,600
Ryo-san.

215
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,520
The bill.

216
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,680
To think he'd try to eat something
else without even realizing it!

217
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,260
He must be nearing his limit by now.

218
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,980
Currently at 195.

219
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:47,340
There are 105 left.

220
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,520
Looks like Reiko wins this one.

221
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,240
We can't let our guard down.

222
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:55,240
When money's involved,
Ryo-chan has an unbelievable power.

223
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:58,340
Reiko's worries came true.

224
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,740
One million yen!
It's all for one million yen!

225
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:07,220
Senpai showed an incredible final push,

226
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:12,980
and on the final day, only one is left.

227
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:17,000
The million yen is ours!

228
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:34,000
So there's just over an hour
left until the time limit.

229
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,700
Senpai's victory is a foregone conclusion,
isn't it.

230
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:41,380
I'll take my time eating the last
one right in front of you two.

231
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:47,060
I'm getting the 1 million yen in cash,
so you'd better get it ready now.

232
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:50,320
Fine, I'll go to the bank and withdraw it.

233
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,580
I'll go with you too.

234
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:55,660
Carrying a large amount of cash around is dangerous,
after all.

235
00:13:56,180 --> 00:13:58,260
Well then, I'm off to patrol.

236
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,020
Hurry back, you hear?

237
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:09,980
Now then, 1 million yen...
what should I spend it on?

238
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:11,920
I'm back!

239
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,900
What, is nobody here?

240
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:23,720
Is Ryotsu slacking off again?

241
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:27,220
If we leave watermelons out here like this,
they'll get warm.

242
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:34,260
As expected,
watermelon has to be chilled like this.

243
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,440
Ohara-kun.

244
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:40,780
Did you find him, Ohara-kun?

245
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,300
Kojima, long time no see.

246
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,300
Could you hold onto this for a moment?

247
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:47,780
Watermelon.

248
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:50,520
I'm counting on you.
I'm going to use the restroom.

249
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:53,820
Did he get a stomachache from
eating too much watermelon?

250
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:55,860
Thief!

251
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:56,380
What?

252
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,240
Hey, did Ika fall asleep?

253
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,120
Reiko still hasn't come back?

254
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:16,160
There's no more.

255
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,140
Where did she go?

256
00:15:23,100 --> 00:15:24,780
So it was here all along.

257
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,680
Shall we get ready to eat?

258
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,380
That's refreshing.

259
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,480
What do you think you're doing?

260
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,200
That's my line.

261
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,560
Who are you?

262
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:37,060
What are you doing here?

263
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,420
Hand it over to us.

264
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:42,040
What? Why would I have
to hand it over to you?

265
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:43,480
Hand it over.

266
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,300
As if I'd hand it over!

267
00:15:44,300 --> 00:15:46,440
Could it be that this guy

268
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:48,500
isn't one of Reiko's acquaintances?

269
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:49,860
That Reiko...

270
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:52,100
suddenly made paying the
million yen seem worthwhile.

271
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:53,260
You're trying to get in our way, aren't you?

272
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:54,560
Seriously, hand it over.

273
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,760
I'm going to eat this watermelon.

274
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:58,080
No matter what.

275
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,480
Well, the culprit must
have been surprised too.

276
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:03,400
Two police officers suddenly
appeared right in front of him.

277
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,840
We just happened to be passing by.

278
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:07,120
Thank goodness.

279
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,680
Case closed, Ryo-chan.

280
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:16,960
Where's he going? He's not skipping out again, is he?
No, that couldn't be it.

281
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:21,060
Waah! Wait! Kojima, what's wrong?

282
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:31,080
Ohara, that man left the thing with you and ran off with it.
That watermelon? That's not a watermelon at all, it's a bomb!

283
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:33,480
If you give it a shock, it'll explode!

284
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:42,100
The one fleeing with a bomb is

285
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:45,080
Senior Patrol Officer Kankichi
Ryotsu of Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box

286
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:47,180
secure him immediately upon sighting.

287
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:50,120
Also, the bomb in Senior Patrol
Officer Ryotsu's possession

288
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:52,760
may explode if subjected to a strong shock.

289
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,360
Exercise extreme caution.

290
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:59,100
He was transporting it to headquarters
after seizing it in a case.

291
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:02,360
But then he suddenly
needed to use the restroom.

292
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:03,880
So that's what happened.

293
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:05,900
Yes, if we spot the senior officer,

294
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,920
we were told to make sure he
absolutely does not eat the watermelon.

295
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,860
That's right, it's a bomb.

296
00:17:09,860 --> 00:17:10,980
Reiko!

297
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,360
Hey, Reiko, are you watching?

298
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:15,600
Ryo-chan!

299
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:18,000
I'm going to eat the last watermelon now,
you hear?

300
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,180
I've even prepared the goods
so you can't complain later.

301
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:21,740
So you can't keep quiet about it.

302
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,160
I've got a clock ready, too.

303
00:17:24,740 --> 00:17:25,300
Where is it?

304
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:27,200
It's Ryo's senior's room.

305
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,900
So you can't claim the camera was broken.

306
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:31,800
I'm filming video as evidence, too.

307
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:34,540
Reiko, you'd better pay the 1 million yen,
no matter what!

308
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,020
Bon appétit!

309
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:41,340
Who's calling at a time like this?

310
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:46,140
Hello? Ryo-chan,
don't you dare cut that watermelon!

311
00:17:46,140 --> 00:17:48,480
Reiko, so you were watching after all.

312
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:51,400
Interfering at this stage is unseemly!

313
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:55,160
No, that's not it.
That watermelon is a bomb!

314
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:57,700
Well, I suppose it's a bomb to you.

315
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,880
The moment I eat that watermelon,
your 1 million yen goes flying.

316
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:04,400
That's not what I mean!

317
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:07,400
Stalling won't do you any good.

318
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,840
This watermelon!

319
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:10,500
Ryo-chan!

320
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:14,540
Well then,
farewell to my days full of watermelon.

321
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,800
Yes!

322
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:19,820
What?

323
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,040
Secure him!

324
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,100
What are these guys?!

325
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,460
You've secured him!

326
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,320
You, you!

327
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:41,940
Reiko's really gone and mobilized
the riot police just to block me.

328
00:18:41,940 --> 00:18:46,080
She's that desperate not to pay a million yen?
And she's rich!

329
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:46,940
Ryotsu!

330
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:48,840
Chief!

331
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:55,580
Wait, Ryotsu! Hand that over quietly!

332
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:58,460
Are you really going to
side with Reiko too, Chief?

333
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:02,260
What are you talking about?
That's not just a watermelon!

334
00:19:02,660 --> 00:19:06,220
Of course it is. If I eat it by one o'clock,
I get a million yen!

335
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:08,840
What nonsense are you babbling about?

336
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:10,880
You mustn't eat that thing!

337
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:13,100
You're the one who
doesn't make sense, Chief!

338
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:15,440
What else am I supposed to do
with a watermelon but eat it?

339
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:18,080
Hurry, or it'll blow to pieces!

340
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:22,100
That's why you cut watermelon into pieces
with a knife before eating it, right?

341
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,200
Just give it back already!

342
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,320
No way!

343
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,520
Unicorn

344
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:53,280
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

345
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:56,880
What the hell is this guy?
Isn't that a watermelon? What's going on?

346
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,560
Police! Let's head back.

347
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,800
Emergency call! Emergency call!

348
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,960
The bomb is on the truck
loaded with watermelons.

349
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:23,840
Where's the watermelon
that was just brought in?

350
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,600
Then it's over there.

351
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:31,120
Which one? Which one is it?

352
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,400
This is a pain.

353
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,560
What are you doing?

354
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:41,820
This is an emergency! Shut up!

355
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:53,420
S-senpai! Stop! Yaaah!

356
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,040
The last one!

357
00:20:55,280 --> 00:20:56,640
Chooryaaa!

358
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:57,520
Aaaaah!

359
00:21:01,380 --> 00:21:04,780
What's going on?
I told you one of them was the real deal!

360
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:08,480
W-wait, now that I think about it,
the watermelon-smashing event next door...

361
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,320
Right! Got it!

362
00:21:10,260 --> 00:21:11,740
Watermelon smashing?

363
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:12,980
We have to stop it!

364
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:13,440
Yes!

365
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:22,880
It's time for the watermelon smashing,
with a hundred people lined up!

366
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:25,640
Now, how many of them will
manage to break the watermelon?

367
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,980
Go ahead!

368
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:37,820
Well then, let's have everyone
bring their wooden swords down now.

369
00:21:37,820 --> 00:21:38,700
Stop it.

370
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:48,080
It didn't explode, did it?

371
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:48,880
Phew, saved.

372
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:53,040
Then let's give those who
didn't crack it another chance.

373
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:54,140
One, two...

374
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,600
There's still someone who
hasn't cracked theirs yet.

375
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:06,060
Come on,
let's have them keep at it until it cracks.

376
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:17,020
Damn it!

377
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:20,400
Well done, Ryotsu!

378
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:22,360
I'm the one who's going
to eat this watermelon.

379
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:23,740
What?

380
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,460
It's exactly one o'clock now.

381
00:22:28,970 --> 00:22:30,700
Damn, I didn't make it in time.

382
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:36,360
It's just a regular watermelon

383
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,060
What's going on here?

384
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:40,020
Maybe Honey tricked us.

385
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,040
What?

386
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:43,700
Then what about the -

387
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:47,700
So we were all dancing to the
culprit's lies and obstructing me?

388
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:49,620
Sorry, senpai.

389
00:22:49,620 --> 00:22:51,400
In that situation,
there was no choice, was there?

390
00:22:51,820 --> 00:22:55,060
"No choice" doesn't cut it!
That could have cost us one million yen!

391
00:22:55,060 --> 00:22:56,440
What are you going to do about it

392
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,540
If it weren't for the interference,
I'd have been eating it by now.

393
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:05,400
Welcome back.
The watermelon's nice and chilled.

394
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:10,220
Then if you eat this watermelon within five minutes,
I'll count it as a success.

395
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:13,240
Really? Alright, I'll go get the knife.

396
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,660
There's another watermelon here too!

397
00:23:15,660 --> 00:23:18,480
It's the one I chilled at
the outdoor tap earlier.

398
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,280
So you brought it here, Terai.

399
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:23,400
But this is the watermelon I chilled.

400
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:24,160
What?

401
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:28,060
When I went back to the police box earlier,

402
00:23:28,060 --> 00:23:32,120
it was on the desk,
so I took it to the outdoor tap.

403
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:34,540
My watermelon should
have been there, though!

404
00:23:34,900 --> 00:23:37,420
It already seemed chilled enough, so

405
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:40,180
I put it back on the desk.

406
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:46,360
So then, this watermelon is...

407
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:47,760
Thank you for the food. Let's eat.

408
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:59,880
That's quite a lot... the 1 million yen is

409
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:02,580
I hate extras like this!

410
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:17,160
Haa, summer has come again this year.

411
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,760
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here.

412
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:23,060
Haa, summer has come again this year.

413
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:25,180
It's here, it's here,
it's here, it's here, it's here.

414
00:24:30,860 --> 00:24:33,940
Big bosoms, small bosoms,
the small-bosomed ones.

415
00:24:33,940 --> 00:24:36,060
Agisabel

416
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:40,900
Summer has come again this year.

417
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:46,900
Summer has come again this year.

418
00:24:48,640 --> 00:24:51,640
Big waves, small waves, the small ones.

419
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:55,240
Falling on the southern wind.

420
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:58,300
Big behind, small behind,
the clingy kind, about that size.

421
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:25,220
Bakusa de

422
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:32,320
Whoa! I've gotten smaller!

423
00:25:32,820 --> 00:25:35,660
I should've known it was your doing again,
Kayama Rika!

424
00:25:35,900 --> 00:25:39,120
Damn it! Getting back to the police
box in this body is gonna be a pain!

425
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:40,940
So what do you want, kid?

426
00:25:41,220 --> 00:25:43,480
Me, a fairy?

427
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:46,780
No! Little Ryotsu is the fairy!

428
00:25:47,140 --> 00:25:47,760
Nice to meet you!

429
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:50,780
That's Kame-ari over there,

430
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,120
well, I'm sure there's a turtle, kame-ari!

431
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:59,280
Come on, everyone, to our town!

432
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

